 "_comment": "The shared dry-country set (make_dry_country.py). Terrain cells are opaque, pieces are overlays (magenta = clear); cells are [x, y] in 16 px units. dry: plain first, then variations. N..sTRBL: dry ground on Ekat's grass, the dual grid of Ekat's marsh set. road_*: the cell-based road on dry ground (build.py path_tile keys). cane = encounter grass. salt / salt_dry: Route 24's salt crust. v2: dry_grass is tall dry grass (encounter grass) ringed by dry[0]'s pixels; four dual-grid sets on dry ground (patch inside, dry[0] outside), each <prefix> (its C fill: a cell or a list, plain first) + <prefix>_N ... <prefix>_sTRBL with Ekat's corner keys: cane_wall (blocking cane-field backdrop, its stalk face on the south), salt (C = the salt crust cell), red_earth, gully (an eroded gully, its wall face on the north side). v3: rock_wall (+ rock_wall_N ... sTRBL), a blocking bedrock wall with a 14 px cliff face on its south side (its own geometry: the edge 15 px from an in-corner); dry_grass is now a continuous tall-grass fill and dry_grass_N ... sTRBL its ragged border on dry ground. rock_wall_face / _face_l / _face_r / _face_il / _face_ir: the face-extension cells under the wall's south edge (make_dry_country.face_cells gives the rule). rock_wall is a list like dry: the plain fill, then crack, slab and weathered variations.",
